  "route": "original",
  "notes": "Backlog game, picked from RAWG's most-added list for its year (docs/PLAN.md section 2 ordering). StrategyWiki has no separate Dark Arisen guide: the title redirects to its \"Dragon's Dogma\" page, which is at completion stage 2. Its Table of Contents lists a Walkthrough with 16 parts, but only First Steps and Cassardis, The Encampment, Main Quests of Part 1 and Main Quests of Part 2 are written (plus Achievements and trophies and the Table of Contents), so it was not used. dragonsdogma.fandom.com has a \"Dragon's Dogma: Dark Arisen\" page with about 48 linked pages, including \"Bitterblack Isle\" and \"Dark Arisen: Quests\"; names only were looked at, nothing copied. The Steam schema calls the app \"DUNE\" (an internal codename); the store list confirms app 367500. None of the 59 Steam achievements are hidden, but the story ones read like spoilers, so they were split into an early and a late story chapter by name; the split point (after \"The Message\") is a judgement call. RAWG lists a playtime of only 7 hours, which looks low."
}
